# MLabs workspace — DEFAULT-DENY (AX-1 · NEXUS:M-109).
# Nothing at this root is tracked unless a `!` line below names it.
# A new file or folder is PRIVATE until this file says otherwise — the safe failure.
# Every child folder (the instance, each project) is its OWN repository and is
# never tracked here. Do not add exceptions for directories that hold private work.
/*

# ── the structural allowlist — the public repo is exactly this ──
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# The signature layer (AX-1, amended 2026-08-20). These two files are the ONLY
# place in the tracked set permitted to carry the author's name, and the denylist's
# `## SIGNATURE` section is what permits it — by path AND by term, so every other
# private word still blocks inside them exactly as it does anywhere else.
# ⚠️ These two `!` lines and the files themselves belong in the SAME commit: an
# allowlist line with nothing tracked behind it fails the gate's check 3, which is
# the check that catches scaffolding. `git add -A` does both in one step.
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE

!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/PHILOSOPHY.md
!/AXIOMS.md
!/METHOD.md
!/FLOW.md
!/skills
!/skills/**
!/tools
!/tools/**
# The interface engine (T64). Public and generic by construction: it knows the six
# document kinds and no instance, and reaches one only through the adapter it is
# handed at startup. The adapter itself is NOT here — it lives instance-side, which
# is what keeps this directory cedible (`interface:AX-1`).
!/interface
!/interface/**
# ⚠️ The interpreter's residue is NOT excluded here. It is excluded in the LAST block
# of this file, and the reason is the rule this file learned on 2026-08-20: in a
# default-deny allowlist **a `!` line undoes every exclude above it**, so an exclude
# only holds if no re-include follows it.

# The tools' view of the skills: RELATIVE symlinks, committed so a fresh clone has
# working skills with nothing to run first. Only the link — everything else the tools
# write here (settings, local state) stays private by the re-exclusion below.
!/.claude
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills

!/.agents
/.agents/*
!/.agents/skills

# Stage 2+ adds, one line per piece, when the piece exists: templates/.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE INTERPRETER'S RESIDUE — LAST IN THE FILE, AND IT STAYS LAST.
#
# ⚠️ This is a position, not a preference. Every `!` line above re-includes what the
# excludes above it had just removed, so an exclude high in this file is undone by any
# re-include below it — silently, with no error and no diff.
#
# Proven with `git check-ignore -v` on 2026-08-20, and it is how `__pycache__` came
# back three times. The file carried the interface allowlist block TWICE with a set of
# excludes after each. Three measurements:
#     first block alone  -> ignored, its own exclude fires
#     both blocks        -> the SECOND block's exclude fires; the first is dead, because
#                           the second block's `!/interface/**` re-included everything
#                           the first had excluded
#     second block's excludes deleted -> NOT IGNORED, and check-ignore names
#                           `!/interface/**` as the winning rule
# So the copy that LOOKED like residue was the only one working, and tidying by deleting
# the later lines puts the residue straight back.
#
# ⚠️ And the FIRST fix for that was itself wrong, which is why this block exists rather
# than an interface-scoped one: the old bare `*.pyc` sat after every `!` line and so
# covered `tools/` and `skills/` too. Deleting it silently made a stray `.pyc` anywhere
# else trackable — measured, not assumed. **A narrowing that looks like a tidy-up is the
# shape this file must never acquire**, since what it decides is what goes public.
#
# Unanchored on purpose: any depth, any allowlisted root.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
